[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Efficient

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Performance

[[/SECTION]]

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
A high performance, i.e. less time spent on the CPU, should be preferred in order to conserve energy and reduce impact on the entire system.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Low Resource Usage

[[/SECTION]]

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The editor's memory usage should be appropriate, so it does not impact the system and/or other programs. Also the editor should run on resource-constrained devices.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Low Start Up Time

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Accessible

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Intuitive & Simple

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Non-Prioritization of Input Methods

[[/SECTION]]

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The editor shall not prioritize any arbitrary input method.

Many users have different needs for how they like to interact with their editor. Some prefer to not use a mouse at all, while others may use the mouse almost exclusively.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Flexible

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Configurable

[[/SECTION]]

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The editor shall be easy and quick to configure. Also the initial entry barrier should be set very low, so that users find it easier to get used to the editor.
<<<

